            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The connections between gastroesophageal reflux, nonallergic asthma and angina pectoris are critically reviewed. Although there is no convincing evidence of a widespread pathophysiological link, such interaction may play a role in selected cases.</AbstractText>
